---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Philosophy — The Operating Principles of OneRishi.in"
  description="Operating principles on high-agency generalism, tangible execution over abstract strategy, and the synthesis of technology with literate storytelling."
>
  <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
    
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-14 pb-8 border-b border-[#1B1B18]/15">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2 text-[#1F3A3D]">
        <span class="font-sans text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#1F3A3D]">
          Ethos &amp; Convictions
        </span>
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C1592B] inline-block"></span>
        <span class="font-sans text-[11px] text-[#1B1B18]/60 font-medium">Doctrine Vol. 04</span>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 items-baseline">
        <div class="lg:col-span-8">
          <h1 class="font-serif text-[42px] sm:text-[54px] text-[#1B1B18] tracking-tight leading-none font-normal">
            Philosophy
          </h1>
          <p class="font-serif text-[22px] sm:text-[26px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal pt-2 leading-snug">
            Why I build the way I do.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-4 text-left lg:text-right">
          <p class="font-sans text-[14px] text-[#1B1B18]/70">
            A defense of high-agency generalism, unabstracted craft, and direct human communication.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
      
      <!-- Sticky Sidebar Navigation (3 cols) -->
      <aside class="hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3">
        <div class="sticky top-28 space-y-6 font-sans">
          <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-[#E6E1D8] rounded-lg shadow-sm space-y-4">
            <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-[#1F3A3D] uppercase tracking-wider block">
              Chapters
            </span>
            <nav class="space-y-2 text-[13px]">
              <a href="#myth-of-specialization" class="text-[#1B1B18]/80 hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors flex items-center justify-between group">
                <span>01. The Myth of Specialization</span>
                <span class="text-[#1F3A3D] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
              </a>
              <a href="#execution-over-theory" class="text-[#1B1B18]/80 hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors flex items-center justify-between group">
                <span>02. Execution Over Theory</span>
                <span class="text-[#1F3A3D] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
              </a>
              <a href="#youth-perspective" class="text-[#1B1B18]/80 hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors flex items-center justify-between group">
                <span>03. Youth-Led Velocity</span>
                <span class="text-[#1F3A3D] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
              </a>
              <a href="#core-tenets" class="text-[#1B1B18]/80 hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors flex items-center justify-between group">
                <span>04. What I Believe</span>
                <span class="text-[#1F3A3D] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
              </a>
            </nav>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 border border-[#E6E1D8] bg-[#F0EDE8] rounded-lg space-y-1">
            <span class="font-sans text-[11px] font-semibold text-[#C1592B] uppercase tracking-wider block">Field Note</span>
            <p class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#1B1B18]/80 leading-relaxed">
              True craft thrives when the builder refuses to partition their brain between distribution and delivery.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Center Prose Column (9 cols, max-w-[720px]) -->
      <article class="lg:col-span-9 max-w-[720px] space-y-14 font-sans text-[#1B1B18]/85 text-[16px] leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Opening Proem -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <p class="drop-cap">
            Over the past decade, the software industry engineered a comforting lie: that greatness is forged through hyperspecialized abstraction. Product managers write tickets about systems they have never deployed; growth marketers buy ad clicks for applications they do not comprehend; designers sketch utopian canvases detached from database realities.
          </p>
          <p>
            I reject this artificial segregation of labor. When you break the direct conduit between the machine's pulse, the narrative's soul, and the end-user's sensory experience, you produce sterile, forgettable software. OneRishi.in exists as a living workshop to prove that high-agency generalism is not a relic of the past—it is the ultimate modern leverage.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Chapter 1: The Myth of Specialization -->
        <section id="myth-of-specialization" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#1B1B18]/10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
            <span class="font-serif text-[24px] text-[#C1592B]">I.</span>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-[28px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal">The Myth of Specialization</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Corporate software development loves assembly lines because assembly lines make people interchangeable. But transformative consumer artifacts—from the printing press to the personal computer—have always emerged from practitioners who traversed the whole stack of human curiosity.
          </p>
          <p>
            When an engineer deeply understands storytelling, their APIs do not just return payloads; they support real human journeys. When a writer writes production code, their prose drops marketing jargon and speaks with crystalline clarity. By inhabiting both technical architecture and editorial marketing, the feedback loop collapses from quarters into hours.
          </p>

          <!-- SVG Diagram: Silo Tax vs Agency -->
          <div class="my-6 p-6 border border-[#E6E1D8] bg-white rounded-lg flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 space-y-1 font-sans">
              <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-[#1F3A3D] uppercase tracking-widest">Silo Tax vs Agency</span>
              <h4 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal">Compressing the Loop</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#1B1B18]/75 leading-relaxed">
                Direct synthesis removes translation friction. No lossy spec handoffs, no compromised intent.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 flex items-center justify-center p-3 border border-[#1B1B18]/10 bg-[#F7F4EF] rounded">
              <svg class="w-full h-auto text-[#C1592B]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 280 120">
                <path d="M20 95 C 70 95, 80 80, 130 80 C 180 80, 190 65, 260 65" stroke="#1B1B18" stroke-dasharray="4 4" stroke-opacity="0.35" stroke-width="2" />
                <path d="M20 95 C 80 90, 140 30, 260 20" stroke="#C1592B" stroke-width="3" />
                <circle cx="20" cy="95" fill="#C1592B" r="4" />
                <circle cx="260" cy="20" fill="#C1592B" r="4" />
                <text fill="#1B1B18" font-family="Inter" font-size="9" x="25" y="110">Initiation</text>
                <text fill="#C1592B" font-family="Inter" font-size="9" font-weight="600" x="180" y="15">Synthesized Impact</text>
                <text fill="#1F3A3D" font-family="Inter" font-size="8" x="180" y="80">Segmented Silos</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Chapter 2: Execution Over Theory -->
        <section id="execution-over-theory" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#1B1B18]/10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
            <span class="font-serif text-[24px] text-[#C1592B]">II.</span>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-[28px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal">Execution Over Theory</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Strategy decks feel productive because they create the illusion of forward momentum without exposing the author to the terror of the blank editor or a failed production deploy. You cannot fail in a 40-page deck; you can only look thoughtful.
          </p>
          <p>
            I place my trust entirely in artifacts that breathe in production. Working code, published essays, real users hitting actual endpoints, and community members discussing stories. If an idea cannot be forged into a prototype within forty-eight hours, its theoretical elegance is suspect.
          </p>
          <blockquote class="p-4 pl-6 border-l-4 border-[#C1592B] bg-white rounded-r-lg font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] italic shadow-sm">
            “The compiler does not care about your brand frameworks. It compiles, or it refuses. The user is similarly honest.”
          </blockquote>
        </section>

        <!-- Visual Intermission: Photographed Atmosphere -->
        <div class="w-full my-8 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[#1B1B18]/15 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src="/assets/images/philosophy-journal.jpg"
            alt="Tactile photograph of an open journal, mechanical keyboard, and fountain pen on a sunlit studio desk"
            class="w-full h-72 sm:h-80 object-cover hover:scale-[1.01] transition-transform duration-700"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-3 text-right bg-white border-t border-[#1B1B18]/10 font-sans text-[11px] text-[#1B1B18]/70 italic">
            Reflective workspace • Deliberate artisanal craft
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Chapter 3: The Value of Youth-Led Perspective -->
        <section id="youth-perspective" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#1B1B18]/10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
            <span class="font-serif text-[24px] text-[#C1592B]">III.</span>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-[28px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal">The Value of Youth-Led Perspective</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Incumbents constantly confuse pedigree with capability. They mistake institutional inertia for prudence. But the most vital currents in digital culture have never come from boardrooms reviewing quarterly retrospectives—they come from young builders building in public out of obsession, free from legacy debts.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you lack twenty years of “how things are done,” you retain the luxury of asking obvious questions: <em>Why must software look like enterprise spreadsheets? Why are digital tools stripped of literary cadence? Why shouldn't a developer own their entire distribution pipeline?</em> That grassroots energy is the only force capable of keeping digital tools genuinely human.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Monumental Pull Quote -->
        <section class="w-full my-12 py-12 px-6 md:px-12 border border-[#E6E1D8] bg-white rounded-xl text-center relative overflow-hidden shadow-editorial">
          <div class="max-w-[620px] mx-auto space-y-4 relative z-10">
            <span class="font-sans text-[11px] font-semibold text-[#C1592B] uppercase tracking-widest block">
              Core Axiom
            </span>
            <blockquote class="font-serif text-[22px] sm:text-[28px] text-[#1B1B18] italic leading-snug">
              “A great technical architecture with zero audience is a ghost town; a loud marketing campaign for an empty shell is a con. The only sustainable path is building both with equal conviction.”
            </blockquote>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-[#1B1B18]/70 font-sans text-xs">
              <span class="w-6 h-px bg-[#1B1B18]/30"></span>
              <span>Rushal Sharma</span>
              <span class="w-6 h-px bg-[#1B1B18]/30"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Chapter 4: What I Believe (Core Tenets) -->
        <section id="core-tenets" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-8 pt-4 border-t border-[#1B1B18]/10">
          <div>
            <span class="font-sans text-[11px] font-semibold text-[#1F3A3D] uppercase tracking-widest block mb-1">
              Core Tenets
            </span>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-[32px] text-[#1B1B18] font-normal">What I Believe</h2>
            <p class="font-sans text-[15px] text-[#1B1B18]/75 mt-1">Non-negotiable parameters for engineering systems, narratives, and community.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-8">
            <!-- Tenet 01 -->
            <div class="group flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-8 items-start pb-8 border-b border-[#1B1B18]/15">
              <span class="font-serif text-[36px] leading-none text-[#C1592B] shrink-0 font-normal">01</span>
              <div class="space-y-1">
                <h3 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] group-hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors font-normal">
                  Code is a medium of expression, not just a delivery mechanism.
                </h3>
                <p class="font-sans text-[14px] text-[#1B1B18]/75 leading-relaxed">
                  Software syntax carries aesthetic weight. Clean abstractions, thoughtful error boundaries, and elegant data models reflect the exact same intellectual discipline as precise sentence construction. It matters how it is shaped beneath the glass.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Tenet 02 -->
            <div class="group flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-8 items-start pb-8 border-b border-[#1B1B18]/15">
              <span class="font-serif text-[36px] leading-none text-[#C1592B] shrink-0 font-normal">02</span>
              <div class="space-y-1">
                <h3 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] group-hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors font-normal">
                  Audience is earned through consistent utility and honesty, never trickery.
                </h3>
                <p class="font-sans text-[14px] text-[#1B1B18]/75 leading-relaxed">
                  Growth hacks, dark UX patterns, and manufactured urgency yield hollow metrics that vanish the moment an algorithm shifts. Durable patronage comes from delivering uncompromised value, writing lucid prose, and treating the reader's attention with sacred reverence.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Tenet 03 -->
            <div class="group flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-8 items-start pb-8 border-b border-[#1B1B18]/15">
              <span class="font-serif text-[36px] leading-none text-[#C1592B] shrink-0 font-normal">03</span>
              <div class="space-y-1">
                <h3 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] group-hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors font-normal">
                  Small teams with shared vocabulary outpace siloed departments every time.
                </h3>
                <p class="font-sans text-[14px] text-[#1B1B18]/75 leading-relaxed">
                  When two or three builders share deep fluency in user experience, systems programming, and editorial framing, the coordination overhead drops to zero. A nimble squad operates at the speed of thought, out-shipping bloated bureaucracies tenfold.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Tenet 04 -->
            <div class="group flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-8 items-start pb-8">
              <span class="font-serif text-[36px] leading-none text-[#C1592B] shrink-0 font-normal">04</span>
              <div class="space-y-1">
                <h3 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18] group-hover:text-[#C1592B] transition-colors font-normal">
                  Real-world feedback trumps theoretical perfection.
                </h3>
                <p class="font-sans text-[14px] text-[#1B1B18]/75 leading-relaxed">
                  Do not spend months polishing abstractions in the dark. Ship the deliberate v0.1 into the wild. Let reality bend the product. Ten true conversations with an active practitioner will correct more assumptions than a dozen design sprints.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="pt-8 border-t border-[#1B1B18]/15 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-serif text-[20px] text-[#1B1B18]">See these principles in practice</h4>
            <p class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#1B1B18]/70">Examine documented case studies and technical systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <a
              href="/work"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-6 py-2.5 bg-[#C1592B] text-white font-sans text-[13px] font-medium rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity shadow-sm"
            >
              <span>Explore Work</span>
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">arrow_forward</span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="/about"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 bg-white border border-[#1B1B18]/20 text-[#1B1B18] font-sans text-[13px] font-medium rounded-lg hover:border-[#1B1B18] transition-colors"
            >
              More About Rushal
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </article>

    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
